{number: 27}
{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] O come, all ye [D] faithful, [G] joyful and tri-[D] umphant,
O [Em] come ye, O [D] come ye to [A7] Beth-[D] lehem;
[G] Come and be-[C] hold [G] Him [Am] born the [D] King of [Em] an-[D] gels;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G] come, let us adore Him,
O [G] come, let us a-[D] dore Him,
O [C] come, let us a-[D] dore [G] Him,
[C] Christ [D] the [G] Lord.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G] Sing, choirs of [D] angels, [G] sing in exul-[D] tation,
O [Em] sing, all ye [D] bright hosts of [A7] heav'n a-[D] bove;
[G] Glory to [C] God, [G] all [Am] glory [D] in the [Em] high-[D] est;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G] Yea, Lord, we [D] greet Thee, [G] born this happy [D] morning,
[Em] Jesus, to [D] Thee be all [A7] glory [D] giv'n;
[G] Word of the [C] Fa-[G] ther, [Am] now in [D] flesh ap-[Em] pear-[D] ing;
{end_of_verse}
